  "report_discrepancies": [],
  "notes": "The trim holds only the left half of the governmental funds Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances (p4: General, Street, Library columns); the page with Econ Dev, Police, Other Governmental and Total Governmental Funds columns (report page 8) is not in the trim. Governmental receipts/disbursements therefore come from the Statement of Activities - Modified Cash Basis (p2, governmental activities column; cash basis), whose totals tie to the budgetary comparison schedule covering all governmental departments (receipts 741,618 + transfers 4,500 = 746,118 p9; charges 626,374 p11). Roll-forward: 6,354 + 741,618 - 626,374 + 4,500 (net transfers from business-type) = 126,098 = Total Fund Balance (p3). Loan repayments (20,488) are inside the function expenses on p2. Governmental 'Taxes' are property tax per the Statement of Activities (46,121 = General 43,418 + Fire 2,703). Business-type (modified cash) lines from the proprietary funds Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p6), fund columns summed per row (no Total column): 2,119,172 + 1,014,954 + 1,522 - 841,438 - 6,723 - 25,392 - 4,500 = 2,257,595; nonoperating lines printed below the operating totals (outside_printed_total). Proprietary Statement of Cash Flows Total column (p7) used for 'proprietary'. Balance sheet from the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), as FY2023. Detail: budgetary comparison schedule for all governmental departments (pp8-11; zero-actual budget lines omitted); no business-type detail (as FY2023/FY2024). Read pages 1-11 of 11"
}
